---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base
  title="Features — LunaTrack cycle tracking"
  description="Everything LunaTrack tracks today: predictions, symptoms and mood, BBT, ovulation tests, reminders, app lock, and a doctor-ready PDF export."
  path="/features"
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">What LunaTrack tracks</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose">
    This is the shipped list, not a roadmap. Everything here is written to the
    on-device database first — see <a href="/privacy" class="underline">how your data is handled</a>
    for what also leaves the device.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Cycle predictions</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        A calendar estimate of your next period and fertile window, built from the
        cycles you've logged. It is an estimate based on averages, not a diagnosis
        and not a method of contraception.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Symptom and mood logging</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Log flow, symptoms, mood and notes for each day. This is one of the screens
        that carries no ads — see <a href="/privacy" class="underline">how ads work</a> across the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Medication marks</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Mark when you took a medication, day by day. Your medication list itself
        stays on your device; only the daily "took it" mark syncs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Weight</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Track weight over time and see the trend. There is no BMI, no height field,
        and no body classification of any kind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Basal body temperature</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Log BBT and see it charted alongside your cycle, for a symptothermal view
        of your fertility signs. Like predictions, this is awareness only — not
        a diagnosis and not a method of contraception.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Ovulation test results</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Record an OPK/LH strip result. A positive result can corroborate the
        calendar estimate; it never overrides the disclaimer that this is
        awareness, not a "safe day" indicator.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Reminders</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Best-effort local notifications for logging and for product changes.
        Reminders stay on your device and are never uploaded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">App lock</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Require your device PIN or biometric unlock before the app opens. Handled
        entirely by your device; LunaTrack never receives biometric data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Doctor-ready PDF export</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Generate a summary PDF of your cycle, symptom and mood history to bring to
        an appointment. Sexual activity is excluded from it by default. Photos are
        never included — there's no setting for it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-card border border-outline bg-surface-tint p-5 dark:bg-surface-dark-2">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Photo timeline</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Keep photos and videos on a dedicated timeline. Automatic descriptions of a
        photo are off by default — turning that on is a separate choice, made per
        account and per device.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-sm">
    Ready to try it? <a href="/download" class="underline">Get LunaTrack on Google Play</a>,
    or read the <a href="/terms" class="underline">terms of use</a> first.
  </p>
</Base>
